                                    <!-- FAQ Section for AEO -->
                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top: 40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>How much does it cost to build a multi-vendor marketplace app in India in 2026?</h3>
                                        <p>Productised marketplace stack + customisation (our offering): ₹18L–₹32L for a full 4-app suite (customer + vendor + rider + admin) with 8–14 weeks to launch and 100% code ownership. Pure custom build: ₹40L–₹90L+ over 5–9 months. White-label SaaS like Yelo or ShareTribe: ₹4L–₹15L/year but with limited customisation.</p>
                                        <h3>Is a food delivery marketplace cheaper to build than a grocery marketplace?</h3>
                                        <p>Slightly — food delivery total build runs ₹24L–₹42L with productised stack, grocery runs ₹28L–₹51L. Grocery is more expensive because of large catalog UX (8K–30K SKUs vs 50–300 for restaurants), variable-weight item handling, substitution flow, and dark-store inventory sync. The base 70% of the platform is identical.</p>
                                        <h3>How much does a pharmacy marketplace app cost?</h3>
                                        <p>₹31L–₹57L with our productised stack. The vertical-specific add-ons (₹13L–₹25L) cover prescription upload + pharmacist verification, drug schedule classification, optional doctor-consult integration, and CDSCO / state drug controller compliance. Higher regulatory bar than food or grocery — plan compliance from day 1.</p>
                                        <h3>Should I use a white-label marketplace SaaS like Yelo or ShareTribe instead?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes — if you're validating the model, doing under 5,000 monthly orders, don't need customisation, and source-code ownership doesn't matter yet. Most founders should start with white-label SaaS for 6–12 months, validate the model, then move to a productised stack or custom build at ₹18L+. Premature custom builds kill more marketplaces than they save.</p>
                                        <h3>Can I launch in multiple verticals (food + grocery + pharmacy) from one app?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes, but pick one to dominate first. Multi-category apps work technically but split your operations focus across vendor onboarding, rider availability, customer marketing — three completely different motions per vertical. The successful multi-vertical apps we've seen (Swiggy, Dunzo) launched one vertical, won it, then expanded. Don't try to launch all four on day one.</p>
                                        <h3>How long does it take to launch a multi-vendor marketplace app?</h3>
                                        <p>With our productised stack: 8–14 weeks depending on vertical (food fastest, pharmacy longest due to compliance work). Pure custom build: 5–9 months. White-label SaaS: days to weeks. Plan an additional 4–8 weeks of vendor onboarding before public launch — the operations work is bigger than the engineering work.</p>
                                        <h3>Do you give 100% source-code ownership for the marketplace stack?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes — every productised stack engagement transfers 100% of source code, DB schema, design assets, CI/CD config to your private GitHub or Bitbucket as work-for-hire. You can self-host, switch vendor for AMC, or licence the platform onward. The 'productised' part means we customise from a base we've shipped 10+ times — not that you don't own what we build for you.</p>
